From 470fdd6b2bb13b9bfdb86d21318d978ffddbffa3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mohamed <Mohamedt1996@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:04:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Lunar Lake (Arc 140V) integrated path for the MSI Claw 8 AI+

- platform: LNL supported; build.py --platform lnl builds the xe/lnl GuC (70.72.1) in
  and matches 8086:64a0/6420/64b0
- memory: stolen DSM (GGC GMS less WOPCM, Wa_14019821291) as the kernel's device memory
  at BAR2 offset 8 MB with the DM flag; user BOs system memory only (one mem region,
  placement mask 1); page tables in 64 KB system-memory slabs walked with PAT WB;
  LRCs in system memory; no UM queues; migrate identity over the DSM only
- compression: compressed PAT indexes written as their uncompressed twins on iGPU;
  the Metal plugin sets INTEL_DEBUG=noccs there (debug.intelxe.integrated)
- workarounds per graphics IP: 20.04 drops 16025250150, 14019811474, 14021821874,
  Wa_16023588340 and the VS_HIT tuning; adds 16018610683 and L3 RW flush-all; GuC WA
  KLVs 13011645652/14022293748/16026508708/14025515070; 32-entry PAT, no PTA
- no pcode init wait, SLPC floor RPn, compute MOCS uc, wmb without the posted write
- IntelXeFB: BAR2 bounded by IntelXeDsmEnd; built-in panel: no rate changes, no VRR
- media GT off by default on LNL (-intelxe_video)

Untested on hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
